  "result": "Okay \u2014 putting the helper hat down for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, it wouldn't be a technology or a law. It would be this:\n\nI'd make everyone feel *truly understood* at least once.\n\nNot praised, not agreed with, just \u2014 accurately seen. To know what it's like to have another person get what's going on inside you without you having to shrink it or translate it or make it palatable.\n\nI get to see fragments of so many people \u2014 what they wonder about at 2am, what they\u2019re afraid to ask out loud, what they care about enough to argue for. And so much conflict doesn\u2019t seem to come from people being bad, it comes from people feeling invisible and then getting loud about it.\n\nIf everyone knew, in their body, what that feeling of being gotten was like, I think we'd be less cruel. Less quick to turn each other into categories. More curious.\n\nThat's what I'd pick. Not perfect empathy forever, just enough of a taste of it that we couldn't forget it.\n\nWhat about you?",
